  "title": "Kourovka problem 18.116 (main)",
  "statement": {
    "representation": "pdf-text-entry",
    "text": "Given a finite 2-group G of order 2n , does there exist a finite set S of rational\nprimes such that |S| ⩽ n and G is a quotient group of the absolute Galois group of\nthe maximal 2-extension of Q unramified outside S ∪ {∞}?\n   This is true for p-groups, p odd, as noted by Serre.                        P. Schmid",
